From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: clear Elden fixed-slot hotplug capabilities

Elden reports the same 0x0006007f Root Port slot capabilities as Baldur,
even though its Wi-Fi endpoint is fixed. Extend the existing HPC/HPS
clear to Elden so the PCI PM core can consider bridge D3. Leave other
platforms unchanged. The resulting deeper suspend path needs device
validation.

Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/tree/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0214-pci-qcom-baldur-disable-slot-hotplug-capabilities.patch
Signed-off-by: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -372,7 +372,8 @@
 	 */
 	val = readl(pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
 	val |= PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_NCCS;
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur") ||
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden"))
 		val &= ~(PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPC | PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_HPS);
 	writel(val, pci->dbi_base + offset + PCI_EXP_SLTCAP);
 
